--------------------------------------------------------------------
FINDINGS (do not block this attempt; for the lead's adjudication/backlog)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
FINDING 1 (criterion 2b, test-hygiene, insights/trends_test.go:789-799):
  TestCalculateSpendingVelocity_MonthProjectionIdentity has a 60-second-per-
  month flake window. When time.Now() falls in [monthStart, monthStart+60s)
  the d1 clamp yields monthStart+1min, which is AFTER now, so the -280 row
  falls outside SpendingVelocity's [monthStart, now] bucket and the hardcoded
  signedSpent=-580 no longer holds (spentSoFar would be -860). Proven by
  simulation, not by reading alone: 13 failing minutes over a simulated year,
  all at 00:00 on the 1st. A one-line fix (clamp d1 to
  min(monthStart+1min, now) or derive signedSpent from the fixture rows that
  actually land in the bucket) would close it. It does NOT affect today's
  mutant-kill evidence and does not weaken the contract the test pins.

FINDING 2 (criterion 3c, coverage gap, PRE-EXISTING on master):
  The +-5 stable band in MajorExpenseTrends' classifier is pinned by NOTHING
  -- not a committed test, not the oracle. Mutating it to +-0 leaves the
  entire repo suite and all eight oracle probes green, yet it changes what
  users see (a +3% move would read "up" instead of "stable"). Master has the
  same literal and the same absence of a test, so this is not a CB3
  regression; it is a V3-promotion candidate (one fixture with
  current/previous = 103/100 asserting "stable" and 106/100 asserting "up").

FINDING 3 (spec wording, no code impact): Amendment CB3-c bullet 3 says
  "Direction derives from the SIGN OF ChangeAmount (up / down / stable)",
  while the same amendment's context and the worker's implementation derive
  Direction from ChangePercent through the unchanged +-5 band -- so a
  sub-5% positive change reads "stable", not "up". The two readings differ
  only inside the band. I verified the safe part empirically (property probe
  above): Direction NEVER contradicts the sign of ChangeAmount; "stable" only
  ever appears inside the band. Recommend the spec text be reconciled with
  the band so the next enumeration does not reopen it.
